  id: Scene13_FAQ_3
  speaker: WATTSON
  text: Georg Simon Ohm was a German teacher and physicist, born in 1789. He built
    much of his own equipment, measured patiently for years, and published this relationship
    in 1827. The unit of resistance, the ohm, is named in his honour.
